## Context

Raid SKILL.md Phase 6 (lines 87-111) restates the 6-step verify pipeline that
verify/SKILL.md already defines. This 25-line copy rots when verify evolves and
costs ~500 tokens per raid invocation for information the agent gets again when
it invokes `/verify`.

The verify chain totals 844 lines across 4 skills (verify 219, verify-adherence
216, verify-gate 232, raid Phase 6 copy 25). Removing the copy from raid reduces
the loaded prompt for every raid by ~3%.

Caveat: the "redundant" text may be load-bearing for raid agents that need to
understand the verify flow before invoking it. Test by running a raid with the
simplified Phase 6 and checking that verify is still invoked correctly.

## Actions

1. Replace raid Phase 6 lines 91-98 with a one-liner: `invoke /verify <pr-number>`.
2. Keep the mood line, per-wave integration review, and the "never merges" invariant.
3. Run a test raid on a small ticket to confirm verify still fires correctly.

## Test

- Raid Phase 6 is under 15 lines (down from 25).
- `/verify` still runs all 6 sub-phases when invoked from a raid.

## Exit criteria

1. Raid SKILL.md Phase 6 delegates to `/verify` without restating its internals.
2. Per-wave integration review section preserved.
3. A test raid completes Phase 6 successfully.
